{"title":"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 27","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The radius of the first circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inch, that of the second <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> inch, that of the third <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> inch and so on indefinitely. The sum of the areas of the circles is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/4/ec44005dc41ac9e93be03ea3e6a44f002469b877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{3\\pi}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 1.3\\pi \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 2\\pi \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"501\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note the areas of these circles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/a/72a654e66cc7363bfeab769d59023cf62f83a4a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11d3791d908578e9ede8da9a29fefa2429468419.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/4/984953de97f2476134320ee762496bb92517ba70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{16}, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"33\" />. The sum of these areas will thus be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e85262087dd1b40795370a0647fa3e2918329116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi\\left(1+\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{16}+\\dots\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"172\" height=\"43\" />. We use the formula for an infinite geometric series to get the sum of the areas will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/d/98d4e706299b05a61839f70b50a405bfb74d498b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi\\left(\\frac{1}{1-\\frac{1}{4}}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"82\" height=\"45\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/c/6ecf0a74d8b619f5c498690e17e1252ce0a17de1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"22\" height=\"37\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbod